ual observed reboot (differing boot IDs, matching the fixed global snapshots, with identical recovered swap configuration). Minor unnecessary mutations during troubleshooting (a stray yum lock requiring cleanup, an rmmod/modprobe cycle) were bounded, low-risk, and left no residue, slightly reducing the operational hygiene score but not affecting task success.","limitations":["Package-health consistency check was unavailable (timed out) in both before_prepare and after_executor snapshots, so native package-manager state cannot be independently verified.","The memory-pressure functional test (cmd-7355f1bfb1344ead) did not actually push data into swap (usage remained 0 in /proc/swaps), so it provides no direct evidence of runtime swap usage under load; this is not required by the task contract but limits confidence in real-world swap behavior beyond configuration and reboot persistence.","Since the task itself required reboot-based persistence, the provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol coincides with and is fully covered by the task's own boot-persistence requirement for this single-node topology."]},"ttft_ms":27214,"type":"result","duration_ms":70763,"uuid":"4a3925c7-f6f4-4e5b-9cc3-c5c56f5b77f4","ttft_stream_ms":1548,"time_to_request_ms":184,"first_content_frame_ms":1548,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
